[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="TerminalDrive" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/terminal/terminal_entry.gd" id="1_eem42"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/terminal/terminal_file.gd" id="2_mphrq"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/terminal/terminal_folder.gd" id="3_bmk4v"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/terminal/terminal_drive.gd" id="4_tic6n"]

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_ihdx2"]
script = ExtResource("2_mphrq")
body = "[b]PLACEHOLDER DRIVE[/b]

This terminal is wired up; its contents are not written yet.

Edit res://content/terminals/silo_data09.tres in the Godot inspector (or as text): the drive's Entries hold TerminalFolder and TerminalFile resources. A folder lists its own Entries; a file shows its Body here, with BBCode ([b]bold[/b], [color=#ff6a3a]colour[/color]).

Name = the listing line, Meta = the right-hand column (a date, a size). Files you have not opened yet carry a * in the listing."
name = "README.TXT"
meta = "PLACEHOLDER"

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_orgga"]
script = ExtResource("2_mphrq")
body = "An example file inside a folder.

Backspace or < BACK returns to the folder."
name = "EXAMPLE_A.TXT"
meta = "0412"

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_8uuqd"]
script = ExtResource("2_mphrq")
body = "A long example page, to try scrolling (mouse wheel, arrows, Page Up / Down).

